gpl: estimate_target_density, carried from OpenROAD #11395 to measure it.

Not our change and not ours to upstream: this is upstream pull request
https://github.com/The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD/pull/11395 as it stood
at the SHA named below, carried here only so the command it adds can be
run against real designs. The study on this branch is what the patch is
for; nothing on this branch is proposed for merge.

What it adds: a read-only Tcl command

  estimate_target_density [-bin_grid_count n] [-overflow f]
                          [-pad_left n] [-pad_right n]

that binary-searches, over the bins of a freshly initialized Nesterov
state, for the target density that would produce the requested overflow
(default 0.1) without running global placement, clamped to
[get_global_placement_uniform_density, 1.0].

What it also does, which its description does not mention: it deletes
the two hunks in Replace::doIncrementalPlace that forced
uniformTargetDensityMode on, so `global_placement -incremental` no
longer silently uses uniform density. The PR's own diff to
src/odb/test/replace_hier_mod1.tcl adds `-density uniform` to three
existing calls, which is that behavior change showing up in a golden
test -- the reason this branch A/Bs the place stage against the
unpatched binary rather than taking the PR's "no existing behavior
changes" at its word.

Carried verbatim, every hunk, including the test files and the CMake
test registration this repo never builds: a rewritten patch would no
longer be the thing under measurement.

How it retires: the `//:bump` that lands on an openroad master carrying
#11395 (merged or abandoned). Applied on top of
OpenROAD 41a28926b92c5c20f41f89e90222a95a820384d2; PR head at the time
of fetch was the-openroad-project-staging:gpl-estimate_target_density.

